    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d54-a13">

                <pb facs="0162" n="144" xml:id="pg144"/>

                <head>[Extract from affidavit of John Malowansky, agent of lessees of Commander
                    Islands.]</head>
                <p rendition="#center"><hi rendition="#small-caps">management; pelagic
                    sealing.</hi></p>
                <p rendition="#center">* * * * * * *</p>
                <p>In 1891 the schooner <hi rendition="#italic">J. H. Lewis</hi> was caught near the
                    islands by the Russian gunboat <hi rendition="#italic">Aleut</hi> and found to
                    have 416 skins on board. I made a personal examination of these skins, and found
                    that from 90 to 95 per cent were those of female seals.</p>
                <p rendition="#center">* * * * * * *</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">John Malowansky.</hi></signed></closer>
                <closer>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-left">Subscribed and sworn to before me <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1892-04-15">this 15th day of April, A. D.
                            1892</date>.</dateline>
                    <lb/>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">[<hi rendition="#small-caps">seal.</hi>]</seg>
                    <signed rendition="#float-right"><hi rendition="#small-caps">Clement
                            Bennett</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Notary
                    Public.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
